This is a minimalist CMake project for text analysis. It provides a complete solution for calculating text statistics: line counts, character counts, and word counts.

Project Architecture

The project is built on a modular principle, with each functional component isolated as a separate library (target):

Main Targets (Solution Components):

ReadingLib (add_library(ReadingLib ...))

Component for reading multi-line text
Implementation: src/reading.cpp
Interface: include/reading.h
CountLinesLib (add_library(CountLinesLib ...))

Component for counting lines in text
Implementation: src/count_lines.cpp
Interface: include/count_lines.h
CountSymbolsLib (add_library(CountSymbolsLib ...))

Component for counting characters (excluding newline characters)
Implementation: src/count_symbols.cpp
Interface: include/count_symbols.h
CountWordsLib (add_library(CountWordsLib ...))

Component for counting words in text
Implementation: src/count_words.cpp
Interface: include/count_words.h
MyApp (add_executable(MyApp ...))

Main application
Uses all library components
Implementation: src/main.cpp
unit_tests (add_executable(unit_tests ...))

Executable for unit testing
Uses Catch2 framework
Implementation: tests/test_basic.cpp

Component Functionality

reading.cpp:

Reads multi-line text from standard input
Supports input termination with empty line
Preserves text structure (newline characters)

count_lines.cpp:

Counts lines based on newline characters (\n)
Includes empty lines in count

count_symbols.cpp:

Counts total characters
Excludes newline characters from count
Works with multi-line text

count_ords.cpp:

Counts words using standard delimiters
Handles punctuation and special characters
Ignores consecutive delimiters

Dependencies:

Catch2 v3.4.0: Unit testing framework
Automatically downloaded via FetchContent
Located in ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/external/


